WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.304 --> 00:00:01.425
(turbine roars loudly)

00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:03.205
(object thunks solidly)

00:00:03.205 --> 00:00:04.248
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:04.248 --> 00:00:05.723
Today we're going to talk about

00:00:05.723 --> 00:00:08.543
how you can deal with loneliness.

00:00:08.543 --> 00:00:09.462
And also as you watch it,

00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:11.689
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:11.689 --> 00:00:13.146
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.338
and put it in quotes,

00:00:14.338 --> 00:00:16.286
so other people can be inspired as well,

00:00:16.286 --> 00:00:18.608
and when you write
something down yourself,

00:00:18.608 --> 00:00:21.890
it's much more likely to
stick for you as well.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:22.771
Enjoy.

00:00:22.771 --> 00:00:26.021
(calm and jolly music)

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:39.584
(moves into soft and airy music)

00:00:40.603 --> 00:00:43.622
- What happens when you're lonely?

00:00:43.622 --> 00:00:44.455
You know,

00:00:44.455 --> 00:00:46.233
when you have this true
feeling of aloneness

00:00:46.233 --> 00:00:48.802
despite being all connected
as we are these days,

00:00:48.802 --> 00:00:50.345
where there's social media everywhere

00:00:50.345 --> 00:00:52.875
where you can follow all your
friends or all your family

00:00:52.875 --> 00:00:54.890
or all the strangers and
celebrities of the world,

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.306
where you can keep
connected to everything,

00:00:57.306 --> 00:01:00.228
but you're not feeling connected.

00:01:00.228 --> 00:01:02.221
Where you feel truly apart from the world

00:01:02.221 --> 00:01:03.611
or apart from others,

00:01:03.611 --> 00:01:06.270
or you're in a place where
you just feel so separate,

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.909
or you feel depressed, and truly alone.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:13.047
You feel a sense of
loneliness in your life.

00:01:13.047 --> 00:01:14.571
It's a big topic today

00:01:14.571 --> 00:01:16.578
because I think a lot of
people feel more of it

00:01:16.578 --> 00:01:18.498
than they've probably ever felt before,

00:01:18.498 --> 00:01:20.468
partially because so much
of what they're seeing

00:01:20.468 --> 00:01:22.941
and connecting with online isn't real

00:01:22.941 --> 00:01:23.774
or it's trumped up

00:01:23.774 --> 00:01:26.375
as the best perfect
rendition of someone's life,

00:01:26.375 --> 00:01:28.478
and you think like "Well
my life isn't that good."

00:01:28.478 --> 00:01:30.715
or you see all these shows on television

00:01:30.715 --> 00:01:32.221
where there's these friends

00:01:32.221 --> 00:01:33.470
and they have all these other friends

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.594
and there's all this
adventure and amazingness.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:36.427
And you think, wow,

00:01:36.427 --> 00:01:37.682
the whole world must be full of extroverts

00:01:37.682 --> 00:01:39.143
who have 50 different friends

00:01:39.143 --> 00:01:42.529
and are dating 12 different
people every single month.

00:01:42.529 --> 00:01:44.767
That's just not real.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.407
And so, we have these unreal expectations

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.393
about our social world as well,

00:01:49.393 --> 00:01:52.694
and sometimes it can make
us feel even more lonely.

00:01:52.694 --> 00:01:54.853
So, what do you do?

00:01:54.853 --> 00:01:58.103
(soft and airy music)

00:01:59.003 --> 00:02:00.957
- A lot of people say "I don't fit in!"

00:02:00.957 --> 00:02:02.640
Well, if you don't fit in to this world,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.026
maybe it's because you're
here to create a new one.

00:02:06.026 --> 00:02:07.296
I didn't know that though.

00:02:07.296 --> 00:02:10.434
So, even when I was studying,

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:14.541
I was reading other books
about the third eye and stuff

00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:15.977
and I felt really alone

00:02:15.977 --> 00:02:20.087
because everybody was
just so left-brained.

00:02:20.087 --> 00:02:24.659
And I'm talking about (laughs)
different galaxies and stuff.

00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:26.050
Okay?

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:26.883
Now,

00:02:27.753 --> 00:02:29.857
this is what I found out

00:02:29.857 --> 00:02:33.337
being a professional alone person.

00:02:33.337 --> 00:02:36.406
(laughs) The first secret

00:02:36.406 --> 00:02:38.807
is that it's okay to be alone.

00:02:38.807 --> 00:02:41.162
Oh my gosh, thank goodness for that.

00:02:41.162 --> 00:02:42.341
Say it again Ralph,

00:02:42.341 --> 00:02:45.258
It's okay to be alone.

00:02:46.302 --> 00:02:50.479
I get over a thousand
messages every single day,

00:02:50.479 --> 00:02:52.562
and a lot of people write
to me saying "Ralph,

00:02:52.562 --> 00:02:56.729
"I just can't seem to find
anybody I can get on with.

00:02:57.654 --> 00:02:59.903
"So I'm alone, and I don't like it."

00:02:59.903 --> 00:03:03.838
(chuckles) It's okay to be alone.

00:03:03.838 --> 00:03:05.458
The reason why a lot of people

00:03:05.458 --> 00:03:08.184
experience a lot of loneliness

00:03:08.184 --> 00:03:12.029
is because they are in
resistance to being alone.

00:03:12.029 --> 00:03:13.779
And that was me.

00:03:13.779 --> 00:03:15.099
Actually, I've got a story.

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:16.011
When I was young,

00:03:16.011 --> 00:03:18.025
my mom was actually very worried

00:03:18.025 --> 00:03:21.332
because she would find
me playing by myself,

00:03:21.332 --> 00:03:24.537
and I would be smiling, right?

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:27.170
So I've always been used to being alone

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:30.291
and being okay with it, right?

00:03:30.291 --> 00:03:32.908
It's okay to be alone.

00:03:32.908 --> 00:03:36.595
Because have you ever been around somebody

00:03:36.595 --> 00:03:38.598
and you never ever see them alone?

00:03:38.598 --> 00:03:41.269
They've always got like a
bunch of friends with 'em?

00:03:41.269 --> 00:03:45.310
They can't put down their
phone for like, two seconds?

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.254
And yeah, I get it.

00:03:48.254 --> 00:03:51.820
Because being alone is frightening

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:54.653
to the majority of the human race,

00:03:55.974 --> 00:03:59.552
because being alone means (gasps) yeah,

00:03:59.552 --> 00:04:02.950
you got to be with yourself,
you got to go within.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.217
A lot of stuff is going to come out.

00:04:05.217 --> 00:04:06.299
That's why a lot of us,

00:04:06.299 --> 00:04:08.473
we want to always be with friends.

00:04:08.473 --> 00:04:11.501
But if you continue just
to follow the crowd,

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:15.210
you will only go as far as the crowd.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.571
- If there are people in
your life, wherever it is,

00:04:17.571 --> 00:04:19.652
try the plus one strategy.

00:04:19.652 --> 00:04:22.760
You're going to go out
to dinner with a buddy,

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.121
maybe it's your only
close friend in the world.

00:04:25.121 --> 00:04:26.908
Ask your closest friend
in the world and say,

00:04:26.908 --> 00:04:30.048
"Why don't you bring someone to dinner?

00:04:30.048 --> 00:04:31.365
"We can just have them there,

00:04:31.365 --> 00:04:33.205
"and we'll make it a, instead
of just the two of us,

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:35.704
"we'll have three at dinner," you know?

00:04:35.704 --> 00:04:38.904
And start introducing one more person

00:04:38.904 --> 00:04:40.647
into your social interactions,

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:43.700
asking them questions, sharing
a little about yourself.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:47.014
And as that happens,
it's not about quantity,

00:04:47.014 --> 00:04:47.887
it's about quality,

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.929
which is why you're starting
with that conversation,

00:04:49.929 --> 00:04:52.446
engaging with real interest in others,

00:04:52.446 --> 00:04:54.177
sharing yourself with them,

00:04:54.177 --> 00:04:56.047
and being okay with that interaction.

00:04:56.047 --> 00:04:58.673
But now, let's just start
amping it up, one plus.

00:04:58.673 --> 00:05:01.613
If you and your spouse are
going out with somebody,

00:05:01.613 --> 00:05:04.169
then ask that couple to
bring another couple.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:08.605
Just get used to enlarging
your social sphere

00:05:08.605 --> 00:05:10.050
a little bit more.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:10.883
Because you know how it is,

00:05:10.883 --> 00:05:13.111
sometimes you do have a social sphere

00:05:13.111 --> 00:05:15.081
but you don't really connect with them.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.193
You know what I mean?

00:05:16.193 --> 00:05:18.472
Maybe you've got like
three people in your life

00:05:18.472 --> 00:05:20.823
and you're like, you know,
you like one of them?

00:05:20.823 --> 00:05:22.435
Well ask all three to bring somebody

00:05:22.435 --> 00:05:23.941
to the next thing that you do,

00:05:23.941 --> 00:05:25.674
and now the odds are increasing

00:05:25.674 --> 00:05:27.846
that you're going to find
somebody to connect with.

00:05:27.846 --> 00:05:29.867
Because one new person to connect with

00:05:29.867 --> 00:05:34.487
can change your outlook,
your mood, your life forever.

00:05:34.487 --> 00:05:37.721
One new person can bring
in a whole new quality

00:05:37.721 --> 00:05:39.008
of energy into your life.

00:05:39.008 --> 00:05:40.276
Just one.

00:05:40.276 --> 00:05:41.109
But you have to be proactive,

00:05:41.109 --> 00:05:41.959
you can't wait and sit there and go

00:05:41.959 --> 00:05:43.110
"I hope, I hope, I hope!"

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.421
You got to invite people
to stuff, you know?

00:05:45.421 --> 00:05:46.539
That's the key.

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:48.509
You got to start inviting people to stuff.

00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:49.896
And so that plus one strategy,

00:05:49.896 --> 00:05:51.769
if you're going to do
anything with another person,

00:05:51.769 --> 00:05:54.007
invite another person along with that,

00:05:54.007 --> 00:05:55.780
you're going to start to see

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.093
that your social sphere grows

00:05:57.093 --> 00:05:59.243
and the odds are you'll find somebody

00:05:59.243 --> 00:06:01.079
in there to connect with.

00:06:01.079 --> 00:06:03.558
- Here's the belief
I'd like you to try on.

00:06:03.558 --> 00:06:07.317
I don't need an excuse to feel good.

00:06:07.317 --> 00:06:08.935
What if I don't need
an excuse to feel good?

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:10.870
I just feel good for no good reason.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.287
How many like this idea, say aye!

00:06:12.287 --> 00:06:15.324
(audience cheers)

00:06:15.324 --> 00:06:16.241
Now notice,

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:18.710
notice when I first said it,

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.359
you guys were kind of
quiet, processing it,

00:06:20.359 --> 00:06:23.200
like "I don't need a reason to feel good?

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.989
"Well, how will I know when to feel good?"

00:06:25.989 --> 00:06:28.447
Some people say that sounds really naive.

00:06:28.447 --> 00:06:29.341
Really!

00:06:29.341 --> 00:06:31.947
Most people don't need
a reason to feel bad.

00:06:31.947 --> 00:06:33.666
"How's it going?"

00:06:33.666 --> 00:06:35.083
"Feel like crap."

00:06:36.607 --> 00:06:37.524
"How come?"

00:06:38.495 --> 00:06:39.411
"Woke up."

00:06:39.411 --> 00:06:41.617
(audience laughs)

00:06:41.617 --> 00:06:45.642
And people go, "I
understand, I understand."

00:06:45.642 --> 00:06:46.475
What if you went up to somebody and said

00:06:46.475 --> 00:06:47.904
"How's it going?" and
they go "I feel so great!"

00:06:47.904 --> 00:06:50.130
"How come?" "I don't
know, I just feel good!"

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.547
You go, "Take that guy
to the psychiatrist."

00:06:52.547 --> 00:06:53.976
(audience laughs)

00:06:53.976 --> 00:06:54.970
Right?

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.791
They're manic, they're crazy.

00:06:57.791 --> 00:07:00.324
But somebody else is depressed
and angry and frustrated,

00:07:00.324 --> 00:07:02.844
you think that's totally normal.

00:07:02.844 --> 00:07:05.699
That's the cultural hypnosis
that we've all been in,

00:07:05.699 --> 00:07:07.516
no matter what country we live in.

00:07:07.516 --> 00:07:09.125
People come to me all the
time in a conference like this

00:07:09.125 --> 00:07:13.292
and they'll go, "Mr.
Robbins, (sighs heavily)

00:07:15.471 --> 00:07:17.975
"I don't know what it is.

00:07:17.975 --> 00:07:21.217
"I just feel down all the time.

00:07:21.217 --> 00:07:24.050
"Why do you think I feel that way?

00:07:25.248 --> 00:07:26.081
So I'll say, "I feel so up!

00:07:26.081 --> 00:07:27.634
"Why do you think I feel
so up all the time?"

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:30.889
"I don't know, maybe it's your body."

00:07:30.889 --> 00:07:33.517
People come up to you and
they go, "Mr. Robbins,

00:07:33.517 --> 00:07:36.809
"I don't know what it
is, but for some reason,

00:07:36.809 --> 00:07:39.315
"I'm angry all the time.

00:07:39.315 --> 00:07:40.991
"Do you know what it is?"

00:07:40.991 --> 00:07:42.129
"Perhaps it's your face."

00:07:42.129 --> 00:07:44.705
(audience laughs)

00:07:44.705 --> 00:07:46.993
See, do we get into
habits of using our body,

00:07:46.993 --> 00:07:49.213
our face, in a certain
way over and over again?

00:07:49.213 --> 00:07:50.046
Yes or no?

00:07:50.931 --> 00:07:53.284
And those produce our emotion.

00:07:53.284 --> 00:07:55.546
Once you're in that state,

00:07:55.546 --> 00:07:58.946
you'll behave in a way that
creates more of that emotion.

00:07:58.946 --> 00:07:59.810
When you're angry,

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:01.877
you'll do things that make you more angry.

00:08:01.877 --> 00:08:03.861
When you're sad, you'll do
things that make you more sad.

00:08:03.861 --> 00:08:04.694
When you're excited,

00:08:04.694 --> 00:08:05.797
you'll do things that
make you more excited.

00:08:05.797 --> 00:08:07.191
How many follow, say aye!

00:08:07.191 --> 00:08:08.140
- [Audience] Aye!

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:11.890
- So the secret is to
build emotional biceps,

00:08:12.776 --> 00:08:13.843
emotional fitness,

00:08:13.843 --> 00:08:16.051
by going in these states
over and over again.

00:08:16.051 --> 00:08:18.409
- The only thing that causes loneliness

00:08:18.409 --> 00:08:20.122
is our own thoughts.

00:08:20.122 --> 00:08:22.034
So for single people,

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:24.867
what happens is we tend to believe

00:08:25.975 --> 00:08:29.975
being in a relationship
would make me happy.

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:31.284
Being in a relationship

00:08:31.284 --> 00:08:34.629
would make me feel complete and whole.

00:08:34.629 --> 00:08:39.155
Being in a relationship
is how to be happiest.

00:08:39.155 --> 00:08:41.059
And as soon as we think that,

00:08:41.059 --> 00:08:44.130
as soon as we create this fantasy

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:47.505
all of a sudden, this
moment is insufficient.

00:08:47.505 --> 00:08:49.414
This moment is lacking.

00:08:49.414 --> 00:08:51.246
This moment isn't good enough.

00:08:51.246 --> 00:08:54.043
And that's what creates our loneliness.

00:08:54.043 --> 00:08:55.317
So paradoxically,

00:08:55.317 --> 00:09:00.033
having a fantasy about what
you think will make you happy

00:09:00.033 --> 00:09:03.118
creates loneliness in this moment.

00:09:03.118 --> 00:09:06.278
And then we constantly end
up searching for somebody

00:09:06.278 --> 00:09:08.186
to love us, someone to be with,

00:09:08.186 --> 00:09:12.325
and that all just
perpetuates the loneliness.

00:09:12.325 --> 00:09:13.377
So in other words,

00:09:13.377 --> 00:09:16.819
what creates our loneliness is the belief

00:09:16.819 --> 00:09:19.986
that a relationship can make us happy.

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:24.723
So if you want to stop feeling lonely,

00:09:24.723 --> 00:09:26.968
you need to question that belief.

00:09:26.968 --> 00:09:28.986
Happiness is what remains

00:09:28.986 --> 00:09:33.184
when we lose the thoughts
that make us unhappy.

00:09:33.184 --> 00:09:34.017
That's it.

00:09:34.987 --> 00:09:37.126
So if you can see that a relationship

00:09:37.126 --> 00:09:40.201
doesn't have the ability
to make you happy,

00:09:40.201 --> 00:09:43.463
then you can stop these
fantasies about it.

00:09:43.463 --> 00:09:46.013
Whether you're in a
relationship or you're single,

00:09:46.013 --> 00:09:49.026
doesn't affect your
happiness, only thoughts do.

00:09:49.026 --> 00:09:51.085
So being single, being alone,

00:09:51.085 --> 00:09:52.484
being by yourself

00:09:52.484 --> 00:09:55.425
doesn't create unhappiness,
only thoughts do.

00:09:55.425 --> 00:09:59.559
So you're not in a disadvantageous
position of being happy.

00:09:59.559 --> 00:10:02.267
You can be happy and fulfilled

00:10:02.267 --> 00:10:05.436
just as easily as somebody
in a relationship can.

00:10:05.436 --> 00:10:07.058
So your life is not lacking,

00:10:07.058 --> 00:10:08.968
you are not missing anything.

00:10:08.968 --> 00:10:12.499
Your life isn't insufficient
just because you're single.

00:10:12.499 --> 00:10:15.124
It's okay, it doesn't mean anything,

00:10:15.124 --> 00:10:19.291
and it absolutely doesn't
mean you can't be happy.

00:10:20.239 --> 00:10:22.175
So if you can see that,

00:10:22.175 --> 00:10:24.803
then watch the loneliness just subside.

00:10:24.803 --> 00:10:25.676
- [Narrator] Nick asks

00:10:25.676 --> 00:10:27.596
"It's lonely as an entrepreneur sometimes.

00:10:27.596 --> 00:10:30.442
"How do you cope with that feeling?"

00:10:30.442 --> 00:10:32.190
- You know, for me, I'm built for it.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:33.304
I want to be lonely.

00:10:33.304 --> 00:10:36.419
I want to struggle and grind

00:10:36.419 --> 00:10:37.720
and have all the pressure.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.443
I'm going to take the
last shot in the game,

00:10:40.443 --> 00:10:42.295
always, every time.

00:10:42.295 --> 00:10:45.433
If you want the audacity
to be a millionaire,

00:10:45.433 --> 00:10:47.029
to be successful, to write books,

00:10:47.029 --> 00:10:48.436
if you want the audacity,

00:10:48.436 --> 00:10:52.522
don't you understand the crap
that comes along with that?

00:10:52.522 --> 00:10:55.061
Like, I wanted the
audacity to be in shape.

00:10:55.061 --> 00:10:57.684
It's come with a lot of crap,
it's been a lot of work.

00:10:57.684 --> 00:10:59.062
But 18 months in, and I'm like,

00:10:59.062 --> 00:11:01.520
and I said this the other
day on my fitness video,

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:02.887
I'm not sure I would do this

00:11:02.887 --> 00:11:04.894
if I saw what I would
look like 18 months later.

00:11:04.894 --> 00:11:07.572
Meaning I'd look a lot better, but dammit,

00:11:07.572 --> 00:11:08.405
I would have been like, really?

00:11:08.405 --> 00:11:10.904
For every single day for 18 months?

00:11:10.904 --> 00:11:12.362
To wake up at four in the morning?

00:11:12.362 --> 00:11:14.026
You know, like I'm going to
be like (grumbles), you know.

00:11:14.026 --> 00:11:14.859
So

00:11:16.357 --> 00:11:17.835
you deal with it

00:11:17.835 --> 00:11:20.728
because it's a very small price to pay

00:11:20.728 --> 00:11:22.502
for all the phenomenal stuff

00:11:22.502 --> 00:11:26.082
that you headline read and you
aspire to and you dream for.

00:11:26.082 --> 00:11:28.524
The problem is most of you
don't want to eat that sh(bleep)

00:11:28.524 --> 00:11:30.198
to get there.

00:11:30.198 --> 00:11:31.410
- For me, developing a strategy

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.025
around solving your loneliness

00:11:33.025 --> 00:11:34.906
really depends on the
type of person you are.

00:11:34.906 --> 00:11:37.756
I think we all have different
needs for being around people.

00:11:37.756 --> 00:11:39.214
For me, I'm more introverted,

00:11:39.214 --> 00:11:41.930
I need to have energy just by myself,

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.505
I need to have time
where I'm in a solo space

00:11:44.505 --> 00:11:45.547
for a good chunk of time.

00:11:45.547 --> 00:11:47.633
If I'm around people too much,

00:11:47.633 --> 00:11:51.367
then I get depleted
and I need to recharge.

00:11:51.367 --> 00:11:53.133
And I think the only caveat

00:11:53.133 --> 00:11:54.425
is when I'm around entrepreneurs.

00:11:54.425 --> 00:11:56.334
When I'm around entrepreneurs,
and I'm helping them,

00:11:56.334 --> 00:11:58.479
we're having an impact, I
can do that all day long.

00:11:58.479 --> 00:12:00.628
But if you're looking
at friends and family

00:12:00.628 --> 00:12:03.064
and social functions, it really drains me.

00:12:03.064 --> 00:12:04.270
And so I think what's really important

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:07.259
is understanding how
much social time you need

00:12:07.259 --> 00:12:08.859
and devising a strategy around it.

00:12:08.859 --> 00:12:11.295
So, as an example, if I'm
around people all day,

00:12:11.295 --> 00:12:12.869
if I'm feeling there's people around me,

00:12:12.869 --> 00:12:13.930
we're having conversations,

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.583
then at night, I don't
need to be around people,

00:12:15.583 --> 00:12:17.186
I'm okay just being by myself,

00:12:17.186 --> 00:12:19.288
relaxing, unwinding, doing some more work,

00:12:19.288 --> 00:12:20.636
you know, whatever I'm doing,

00:12:20.636 --> 00:12:22.826
I'm okay to be solo or just with Nina.

00:12:22.826 --> 00:12:24.928
If I spent the whole day by myself,

00:12:24.928 --> 00:12:27.434
and I haven't had any human
contact beyond, you know,

00:12:27.434 --> 00:12:29.550
Snapchat, Instagram,
YouTube, that kind of stuff,

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:32.301
then I find myself
needing to have to go out,

00:12:32.301 --> 00:12:34.708
whether it's coming to an event
here in Toronto Dance Salsa,

00:12:34.708 --> 00:12:36.485
booking a meeting, going to an event,

00:12:36.485 --> 00:12:39.259
something so that I
have more human contact.

00:12:39.259 --> 00:12:40.221
I think what's really important

00:12:40.221 --> 00:12:42.722
is when you understand how much you need

00:12:42.722 --> 00:12:44.972
that you devise a strategy for it,

00:12:44.972 --> 00:12:47.074
so that it consistently
happens in your schedule

00:12:47.074 --> 00:12:49.813
and that you're not stuck, last minute,

00:12:49.813 --> 00:12:52.181
feeling depressed that
you have nothing to do.

00:12:52.181 --> 00:12:53.903
I think that's where it
can get really scary,

00:12:53.903 --> 00:12:55.697
I think that's when you
can get really lonely,

00:12:55.697 --> 00:12:56.941
really depressing,

00:12:56.941 --> 00:12:59.754
is you know that you're spending
the whole day by yourself.

00:12:59.754 --> 00:13:00.804
You know that at night,

00:13:00.804 --> 00:13:01.875
you're going to have a hard time

00:13:01.875 --> 00:13:03.761
if you haven't had any social contact.

00:13:03.761 --> 00:13:06.875
And then you get there,
you're in the moment at night,

00:13:06.875 --> 00:13:08.548
and you don't have
anybody to connect with.

00:13:08.548 --> 00:13:10.357
Where if you know that
that's part of your pattern,

00:13:10.357 --> 00:13:11.513
you know how much you need,

00:13:11.513 --> 00:13:13.311
then you can sign up for a dance class,

00:13:13.311 --> 00:13:14.749
you can sign up for a meet-up,

00:13:14.749 --> 00:13:17.563
you can book a coffee
appointment with somebody

00:13:17.563 --> 00:13:19.648
you want to get to know,
or hang out with friends.

00:13:19.648 --> 00:13:21.363
And so I think, first of all,

00:13:21.363 --> 00:13:23.625
understanding how much
contact you need with people

00:13:23.625 --> 00:13:25.679
to feel whole, to feel good,

00:13:25.679 --> 00:13:28.343
and then devising a strategy
so it's in your schedule

00:13:28.343 --> 00:13:29.724
and you've planned for it,

00:13:29.724 --> 00:13:32.627
and you don't get caught last
minute on either spectrum

00:13:32.627 --> 00:13:35.962
of having too much or having too little.

00:13:35.962 --> 00:13:37.021
I think when you can figure that out,

00:13:37.021 --> 00:13:40.668
then you'll really combat
loneliness and be happier.

00:13:40.668 --> 00:13:41.887
Thank you guys so much for watching!

